All I know about "site" is that it's the name of one of the columns of
your data frame.  I assumed it was a string
I further assumed that site[i] would be the same for all seven days of
the week for which you're doing the interpolation.

If those assumptions are correct, you could do something like:

    replicate(7, site[i])

as, for example:

    > replicate(7, "El Paso")
    [1] "El Paso" "El Paso" "El Paso" "El Paso" "El Paso" "El Paso" "El Paso"

for all rows 'i' in your original data frame.

If I'm on the wrong track here, you might want to synthesize a small
data frame, just a couple of weeks or so, and show us the before and
after (i.e., the, say, two-line original, and the 14-day, interpolated
version).

